  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">T015  Nepal: Enhancing Inclusive Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights (SRHR) and Livelihood Opportunities of Young PWD</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to improve well-being of young people with disabilities by increasing their equitable access to and uptake of quality and inclusive Sexual Reproductive Health and Rights (SRHR) services and livelihood opportunities. This proposed innovation phase of the project aims to design a prototype that can drive sustainable improvements in the target group&apos;s equitable access to inclusive SRHR services and livelihood opportunities. It will be implemented in 2 municipalities in Western Nepal and comprise 4 stages: (i) Develop deeper understanding (4 months); (ii) Discover and define prototype (4 months); (iii) Prototyping (18 months); (iv) Evaluation and design of scale-up phase (4 months).</narrative>
  </description>
